hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28004","Narrated Abu Kamil, narrated Ibrahim ibn Sad, narrated Ibn Shihab, and Yaqub narrated us, narrated my father, from Ibn Shihab, from Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, from Umm Al-Ala Al-Ansariyyah, she being a woman of their women, Yaqub said: he informed her that she had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Uthman ibn Mazun fell in lodging, Yaqub said: it fell to them in lodging when the Ansar cast lots for housing the Muhajirun. Umm Al-Ala said: Uthman ibn Mazun fell sick with us, so we nursed him until when he died we wrapped him in his garments, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us, so I said: May Allah have mercy on you, O Abu As-Saib, my testimony upon you is that Allah has honored you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what makes you know that Allah has honored him? She said: So I said: I do not know, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for him, certainty from his Lord has come to him, and I hope good for him, and by Allah I do not know, though I am the Messenger of Allah, what will be done with me. Yaqub said: with him, she said: By Allah I will never declare anyone pure after him ever. That grieved me, so I slept and was shown a flowing spring for Uthman, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of that, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is his deed."
"28005","Narrated Abdur-Razzaq, informed Mamar, from Az-Zuhri, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, he said: Umm Al-Ala Al-Ansariyyah used to say: When the Muhajirun came to Madinah, the Ansar cast lots for housing them, so Uthman ibn Mazun fell to us in lodging, then she mentioned the hadith, except that he said: I do not know, though I am the Messenger of Allah, what will be done with me nor with you."
"28006","Narrated Yunus ibn Muhammad, narrated Layth ibn Sad, narrated Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu An-Nadr, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, from his mother, she said: When Uthman ibn Mazun passed away, Umm Kharijah bint Zayd said: You are pure, O Abu As-Saib, your best days are good. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard her and said: Who is this? She said: I am. He said (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): And what makes you know? So I said: O Messenger of Allah, Uthman ibn Mazun. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, Uthman ibn Mazun, we have seen nothing but good, and this is me, the Messenger of Allah, and by Allah I do not know what will be done with me."
